{"header":"<h1>Module <code><span>Eio_utils.Zzz</span></code></h1>","type":"documentation","uses_katex":false,"breadcrumbs":[{"name":"Index","href":"../../../index.html","kind":"leaf-page"},{"name":"eio","href":"../../index.html","kind":"page"},{"name":"Eio_utils","href":"../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"Zzz","href":"#","kind":"module"}],"toc":[],"source_anchor":null,"preamble":"<p>A set of timers.</p>","content":"<div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec module anchored\" id=\"module-Key\"><a href=\"#module-Key\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">module</span> <a href=\"Key/index.html\">Key</a></span><span> : <span class=\"keyword\">sig</span> ... <span class=\"keyword\">end</span></span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>A handle to a registered timer.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec type anchored\" id=\"type-t\"><a href=\"#type-t\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">type</span> t</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>A set of timers (implemented as a priority queue).</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec type anchored\" id=\"type-item\"><a href=\"#type-item\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">type</span> item</span><span> = </span></code><ol><li id=\"type-item.Fiber\" class=\"def variant constructor anchored\"><a href=\"#type-item.Fiber\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span>| </span><span><span class=\"constructor\">Fiber</span> <span class=\"keyword\">of</span> <span>unit <a href=\"../Suspended/index.html#type-t\">Suspended.t</a></span></span></code></li><li id=\"type-item.Fn\" class=\"def variant constructor anchored\"><a href=\"#type-item.Fn\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span>| </span><span><span class=\"constructor\">Fn</span> <span class=\"keyword\">of</span> <span>unit <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> unit</span></code></li></ol></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-create\"><a href=\"#val-create\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> create : <span>unit <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <a href=\"#type-t\">t</a></span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p><code>create ()</code> is a fresh empty queue.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-add\"><a href=\"#val-add\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> add : <span><a href=\"#type-t\">t</a> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Mtime</span>.t <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span><a href=\"#type-item\">item</a> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <a href=\"Key/index.html#type-t\">Key.t</a></span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p><code>add t time item</code> adds a new event, due at <code>time</code>, and returns its ID.</p><p>If <code>item</code> is a <a href=\"#type-item.Fiber\"><code>Fiber</code></a>, you must use <a href=\"../../Eio/Private/Fiber_context/index.html#val-set_cancel_fn\"><code>Eio.Private.Fiber_context.set_cancel_fn</code></a> on it before calling <a href=\"#val-pop\"><code>pop</code></a>. Your cancel function should call <a href=\"#val-remove\"><code>remove</code></a> (in addition to resuming it).</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-remove\"><a href=\"#val-remove\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> remove : <span><a href=\"#type-t\">t</a> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span><a href=\"Key/index.html#type-t\">Key.t</a> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> unit</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p><code>remove t key</code> removes an event previously added with <code>add</code>.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-pop\"><a href=\"#val-pop\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> pop : \u000A  <span><a href=\"#type-t\">t</a> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span><span class=\"label\">now</span>:<span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Mtime</span>.t <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span>[ <span>`Due of <a href=\"#type-item\">item</a></span> <span><span>| `Wait_until</span> of <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Mtime</span>.t</span> <span>| `Nothing</span> ]</span></span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p><code>pop ~now t</code> removes and returns the earliest item due by <code>now</code>. For fibers, it also clears the thread's cancel function. If no item is due yet, it returns the time the earliest item becomes due.</p></div></div>"}